   347	Explicit caching works (13,343 of 13,346 tokens discounted in the archived run) but does
   348	not fit ReAct's pattern: its prefix grows every step, so an object
   349	cached at step *k* covers a shrinking fraction of the prompt at step *k+n*. We did not
   350	measure whether repeatedly rebuilding it pays off; the claim here is only that the
   351	naive use — one fixed cached block — does not apply.
   352	
   353	Resulting statement: **with a short static prefix, prefix caching helps only the
   354	append-only arms, in both providers, and by an order of magnitude more on Anthropic;
   355	with a long enough immutable prefix it helps the compressing arms too (SKILL.state
   356	saves 79 % and Memory 48 %, above). The shrinking of SKILL.state's advantage measured on
   357	Anthropic does not reproduce on Vertex, where 7.9x in tokens remains 7.6x in effective
   358	input.**
