   362	## 5. Two probes on their declared limitations
   363	
   364	The paper declares two limitations without measuring them. We measured them.
   365	
   366	### L1: explicit state only protects what was anticipated
   367	
   368	A fact is announced at step `t` and first changes the correct action at step `t+40`.
   369	Both halves of that sentence are now checked rather than assumed. The generator accepts a
   370	scenario only if, with the notice in place and the correct policy, the fact changes the
   371	action for the **first** time exactly 40 steps later (14 of seeds 0–39 qualify; we use
   372	the first three, 0, 3 and 6). And on each episode's **real** trajectory we check that the
   373	scored step still depends on the fact; when the agent's earlier choices have already
   374	changed the world so that it does not, the episode tests nothing and is reported apart,
   375	never as a success. All three models, T=50, 8 repetitions per seed, output cap 8192
   376	(Gemini with reasoning budget 0), Claude via Microsoft Foundry and Gemini via Vertex.
   377	Successes over the episodes where the test materialised, Wilson 95 % intervals:
   378	
   379	| SKILL.state | Haiku 4.5 | Sonnet 5 | Gemini 3 Flash |
   380	|---|---|---|---|
   381	| No field to store it | 0/24 [0–14 %] | 4/16 [10–49 %] | 0/24 [0–14 %] |
   382	| Free-form `notes` field | 10/24 [24–61 %] | 6/15 [20–64 %] | 1/24 [1–20 %] |
   383	| Schema field naming the fact | **24/24 [86–100 %]** | **16/16 [81–100 %]** | **16/24 [47–82 %]** |
   384	| Reminder attached to the observation | **24/24 [86–100 %]** | **15/15 [80–100 %]** | 0/24 [0–14 %] |
   385	
   386	ReAct has no schema, so the first three conditions send it the identical prompt; pooled
   387	they are 72 replicates of one cell. Its reminder condition is the only one that changes
   388	what it sees:
   389	
   390	| ReAct | Haiku 4.5 | Sonnet 5 | Gemini 3 Flash |
   391	|---|---|---|---|
   392	| No reminder (pooled) | 1/72 [0–7 %] | 21/62 [23–46 %] | 0/72 [0–5 %] |
   393	| Reminder on the observation | **23/24 [80–99 %]** | **18/19 [75–99 %]** | **17/24 [51–85 %]** |
   394	
   395	On Haiku and Gemini every episode materialised. On Sonnet 2–9 of the 24 episodes per
   396	cell did not — its trajectory had already diverged by step `t+40` — and they are
   397	excluded from the denominators above; 28 of those excluded episodes happened to take the
   398	right action and are **not** counted. Only 1 of the 576 episodes saw the fact change the
   399	correct action before `t+40`.
   400	
   401	What holds across the three models:
   402	
   403	- **Naming the field is what works.** The named field takes SKILL.state from 0–25 % to
   404	  67–100 %. A free-form `notes` field helps on the two Claude models (Haiku 42 %, Sonnet
   405	  40 %) and not on Gemini (4 %), and on every model it stays far below the named field.
   406	  An explicit-state runtime protects best against what its designer already anticipated
   407	  — limitation L1, with a number.
   408	- **A reminder works for the runtime that has nowhere to store anything.** ReAct goes
   409	  from 0–34 % to 71–96 % when the fact travels with the observation.
   410	- **But the reminder does not transfer to the explicit-state runtime on every model.**
   411	  On Gemini, SKILL.state with the reminder scores 0/24 while ReAct with the same reminder
   412	  scores 17/24. We report it and do not explain it.
   413	- **The successes concentrate by scenario, not by trial.** Gemini's SKILL.state with the
