   476	
   477	## 6. Instrument and artefacts
   478	
   479	This is the section that separates this from a blog post, and the one that cost us most.
   480	
   481	**Nine artefacts catalogued** in the first block, all with the same signature: an
   482	implicit contract between runtime and model. The runtime assumed something it never
   483	declared, and the result depended on whether the model guessed right. The first three
   484	cost entire grids; **two surfaced in the audit before publication, and both had produced
   485	a written result, with tables and intervals, ready to send**.
   486	
   487	This second block added six more, and they are worth enumerating because they transfer:
   488	
   489	1. **Greedy decoding does not guarantee reproducibility.** The protocol assumed that at
   490	   `temperature=0` seeds are environment instances and one run per cell suffices. The
   491	   same cell repeated five times gives between 0.830 and 0.960. **Three already-written
   492	   conclusions collapsed on repetition**: an environment effect of −5.8 points that
   493	   turned out to be +0.008, a "monotonic" noise curve that turned out flat, and a
   494	   noise estimate of eleven points that turned out to be a tail.
   495	2. **The distribution has a left tail because failures cascade.** Across five runs of one
   496	   cell the sample deviation is 0.052; **excluding the 0.830 outlier** it is 0.012, and
   497	   three runs of the same cell at T=100 give 0.006. We quote both, because the second
   498	   number is conditional on removing the very run that motivates the point. What forces
   499	   repetition is not the ordinary spread: it is the tails.
   500	3. **The runner discarded the model's responses.** It kept the score and the token
   501	   counts, so `correct=False` was an indistinguishable zero: you could not tell whether
   502	   the model lost track of state — what the experiment measures — or miscopied a JSON
   503	   field. With responses retained, adjudicating 45 failures across four traces of one
   504	   cell gives **32 wrong-shelf (71 %), 7 wrong action type (16 %), 5 field-copy errors
   505	   (11 %), 1 unparseable**.
   506	4. **A truncated episode counted as complete.** Aggregation counted files, not steps; an
   507	   episode of 163 steps out of 200 entered the mean. The bias was two thousandths, but
   508	   it was only found because completeness was checked as a matter of routine.
   509	5. **Traces that did not record their own conditions.** For most of this work the traces
   510	   stored no output cap, reasoning budget, provider or responding model ID. Two files
   511	   from the same cell could come from different caps and nothing would say so — which is
   512	   how a −5.8-point "environment effect" survived long enough to be written down. The
   513	   runners now write a conditions header and per-step token usage — but **only runs made
   514	   after that change carry it**. The historical Gemini traces — Table 1 except the
   515	   Stateful re-measurement, the noise table and the environment comparison — do not, so
   516	   their conditions are certified by the filename and the run log, not by the artefact
   517	   itself. Every trace behind the Haiku table, both Stateful re-measurements, the Memory
   518	   control and the prompt-order experiment does.
   519	6. **A probe that measured the wrong pattern.** The cache probe repeated an identical
   520	   request and concluded that Vertex has no implicit cache, while the project's own
   521	   grids recorded 503,600 cached tokens in one episode. The probe was correct; the
   522	   pattern it probed was not the one the experiment uses.
   523	
   524	A third block, found while measuring the second model, contains the most expensive
   525	artefact of the project:
   526	
   527	7. **One of the four arms never ran.** Stateful read its state patch with a non-greedy
   528	   regex that stopped at the first closing brace. Every nested patch — the normal case,
   529	   `{"shelf_contents": {"3": {...}}}` — was truncated, failed to parse, and was dropped
   530	   without a warning: **40 of 5,775 responses on Gemini produced an applied patch, 0 of
   531	   6,000 on Haiku**. What both
   532	   Stateful columns measured is full history plus a state block with no inventory — empty
   533	   on Haiku, and on Gemini holding only the occasional `last_event` (the 40 patches, in
   534	   11 episodes). Its unit test
   535	   used a flat value and passed. It surfaced only because Stateful beat SKILL.state on
   536	   Haiku and we went to the traces to find out why. Re-measured with the parser fixed,
   537	   no change was detected (§3). The first fix was itself incomplete: on Haiku it still
   538	   dropped every patch written in Markdown — 731 of 3,000 at T=200 — which the third
   539	   adversarial review found, not us; a third parser version closed it. A defect that
   540	   changes nothing measurable is still a defect in what the column claims to measure.
   541	8. **A cap one model respects and the other does not.** The summariser's own cap was
   542	   never reached on Gemini and was exceeded in half the summaries on Haiku (§3). A cap
   543	   is not a neutral constant across models; it has to be checked per model, in the
   544	   traces.
   545	9. **Resuming re-paid finished work.** The completeness check counted the conditions
   546	   header as a step, so no episode ever matched its horizon and every relaunch re-ran
   547	   episodes already measured. It was caught on the first relaunch of R2 because a cell
   548	   finished minutes earlier started again.
   549	10. **The traces did not record cache writes.** The client received them; the trace row
   550	    did not store them. In the first run of the prompt-order experiment the arm that
   551	    rewrites its cache every step — the most expensive case — showed ~540 prompt tokens
   552	    per step and looked the cheapest. Those twelve episodes were discarded and re-run.
   553	    The §4 table does not depend on it: it was computed by the grid runner, which counted
   554	    writes.
   555	
   556	11. **A probe that could not fail.** The first L2 scorer counted dependent steps on a
   557	    simulated trajectory and subtracted only deaf actions, and its runner repaired the
   558	    world whenever the runtime returned no action; a runtime that never answers scored
   559	    100 %. It was the section of this draft we had checked least, because its result was
   560	    the cleanest. The fifth adversarial review found it. Re-measured with the decisive
   561	    step read from the real trajectory, explicit state goes from "132 of 132" to 70 of
   562	    72 episodes. L1 had the same world-repairing runner and a second defect of design,
   563	    found by the sixth review: its fact was not delayed in two of its three scenarios.
   564	    It was redesigned and re-measured (§5).
   565	
   566	Items 5 and 6 were found by an **independent adversarial review of this draft against
   567	the raw traces**, not by us. That review also corrected the failure classification
   568	above, the maintenance-event range in §2, the compression factor in §3 and the sample
   569	size in §3. We recommend the procedure, not the anecdote: have something recompute every
   570	published figure from the artefacts, without access to the prose that justifies it.
   571	
   572	Why traces matter, verbatim from one episode: at step 12 the model stores the SKU of a
   573	different pallet; at step 16 it asserts *"Shelf 0 (SKU-F, stored in step 12)"* when it
   574	had itself stored SKU-B there. **The early error contaminates later decisions** — and
   575	that, not sampling noise, is what produces the tail.
   576	
   577	**The transferable claim**: the paper treats the runtime as neutral infrastructure — a
   578	merge operator, a patch format, a schema, a prompt order. In this project, individual
   579	runtime decisions moved results by amounts comparable to or larger than the difference
   580	between the methods being compared: the schema field decides 0 % versus 67 % on the
   581	dependent step (§5), and a parser that silently dropped state patches decided what one
   582	of four arms measured until it was fixed (§6, item 7). We have not measured every such
   583	decision, so we make no claim about a general range.
   584	
   585	**Repository artefacts**: environment with fidelity flags, per-step traces, completeness
   586	verifier, a density meter that does not call the API, truncation counters, per-episode
   587	checkpointing and end-to-end cache accounting — except in the L1 aggregates, whose cost
   588	fields ignored cache reads and writes until the last re-measurement; its per-step traces
   589	record them and are the source to use.
   590	
   591	---
   592	
   593	## 7. Limitations
   594	
   595	- **`gemini-3-flash-preview` may not be their `Gemini-3-Flash`.** Declared as a risk
   596	  from the outset. Vertex returns the responding model ID on every call and it is
   597	  recorded per step, but not in the traces measured before that change. The Anthropic
   598	  client did not copy it until the last Stateful re-measurement: from then on — its 30
   599	  episodes and the prompt-order experiment — every step records
   600	  `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`; the earlier Haiku traces record only the requested alias
   601	  in their header.
   602	- **A reimplemented environment is not their environment.** We matched what their
   603	  appendix allows us to compare, and the remaining differences are in §2. The shelf
   604	  choice in `Store` still awaits an answer from the authors.
   605	- **Our Memory is not comparable to theirs.** Our summariser compresses fourteen times
   606	  more (5,770-token mean prompt against their 84,364 at T=200).
   607	  What we measured is our summarisation policy, not "summarisation" as a category.
   608	- **We have not proven the environment gaps have no effect.** The measured difference is
   609	  +0.009, with an interval of roughly −0.040 to +0.057 (§2): no change was detected, and
   610	  effects of several points in either direction remain compatible. The same caveat
   611	  applies to the three lowest noise levels in §3.
   612	- **Cell sizes are not uniform.** Nineteen cells carry 15 runs; ReAct at T=200 carries
   613	  19, unbalanced across seeds (3/3/7/3/3). Five of its episodes exist only as
   614	  aggregates, without traces.
   615	- **Cost figures price input only**, and the caching results depend on the length of the
   616	  static prefix (§4).
   617	- **The probes share cap and design across models, not decoding.** Both were re-measured
   618	  on all three models with the corrected runner (§5); Gemini runs with temperature 0 and
   619	  reasoning budget 0, Claude without either setting.
   620	- **One environment.** The second (Software Repository) was retired because it could not
   621	  measure what it was built for, not because the arms scored alike — they did not
   622	  (Haiku: SKILL.state 0.974, ReAct 0.895; Sonnet: 0.876 and 1.000, 9 episodes each). Its
   623	  dependency always sat exactly two steps after the event that created it, so it had no
   624	  delayed relevance to measure (`docs/resultados-bloque1.md`, §4.ter). We do not
   625	  attribute the score differences above to rule or routine steps: a separate diagnostic
   626	  sample of three episodes per arm shows both kinds of failure, and the nine-episode
   627	  cohorts themselves were not adjudicated.
   628	- **SKILL.state's ceiling depends on the model.** At 1.000 with zero variance on Gemini
   629	  the task did not discriminate at the top; on Haiku it does (0.958 at T=200), and the
   630	  failure is in writing the state (§3). Two models are not enough to say which models
   631	  make that error.
   632	- **Stateful has been re-measured only at T=50 and T=200**, with parser version 2 on
   633	  Gemini (which applied 3,748 of 3,750 of its patches) and version 3 on Haiku. The
   634	  intermediate horizons of Gemini's Table 1 keep the defective measurement, marked as
   635	  such.
   636	- **Haiku and Gemini do not share decoding settings** (§3): the cross-model differences
   637	  are between two configured systems, not two models under identical conditions.
   638	- **Haiku's Memory column mixes the summarisation policy with summary truncation** (§3);
   639	  the control arm has n=9 and bounds the effect at T=50 only.

